      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="msv__faq">
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do Irish citizens need a visa for Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">No. Irish citizens have EU freedom of movement rights. You can live in Spain indefinitely without a visa—just residency registration. Simply move and register with local authorities (Oficina de Extranjería or Town Hall). No visa application needed.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What is the registration process for Irish residents?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Register at your local Oficina de Extranjería (Immigration Office) or Town Hall with your passport, proof of accommodation (rental/property), and proof of income (pension, employment). You'll get a certificate of registration (Certificado de Inscripción). Process takes 2-4 weeks.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Can I access Irish pension in Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Yes. Irish pensions continue to be paid abroad. You can receive them in Spain. However, you must notify the Irish Revenue and comply with Spanish tax obligations. The EU-Spain healthcare agreement allows Irish pensioners to access Spanish healthcare via the S1 form.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ What is the S1 form for Irish pensioners?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">The S1 form entitles Irish pensioners to free healthcare in Spain through the public system. You must be receiving an Irish pension. Apply through the Department of Enterprise, Trade and Employment. Once approved, you register with Spanish healthcare and access NHS-equivalent services.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Do I need to file Irish taxes if I move to Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">You become non-resident for Irish tax if you're not present 183+ days per year and have no Irish connections. Once non-resident, you only pay Irish tax on Irish-source income (Irish property, Irish pensions). Notify Revenue of your departure. You also file Spanish taxes as a Spanish resident.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="msv__faq-item">
          <div class="msv__faq-q">❓ Can Irish citizens buy property in Spain?</div>
          <div class="msv__faq-a">Yes, as EU citizens you can buy property freely without golden visa requirements. Same process as Spanish citizens. You'll need NIE (Número de Identidad de Extranjero) to buy property. Property ownership doesn't require visa or residency—it's a separate transaction.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
